    "This technology refers to put various photos and pictures to glass, to draw and then to shoot by camera. For the scene which they can't actualize or its actualizing process might be dangerous, we handled them with matte painting. As computer technology gets advanced, it is developed to digital matte painting, it can play a pivotal role of computer graphic technology.": 2,
    "To stare candle light for a long time and avert your eye suddenly, the candle seems to remain before your eyes. That's because appearance of objects seen through the eyes remains in the brain for a very short time. We call it 'afterimage effect'. To place the black film between paintings, to turn picture quickly between narrow gap, continuous action were much more clearly exposed. This principle is applied to moving image such as movie, animation. visual toy device made with these afterimage effects is just 'Zoetrope'.": 2,
    "After completing mission that includes the communication with fictional alien civilization, coexistence and cooperation, space crew ride starship to enter station, riding space elevator to return galaxy academy on earth. To understand curiosity about space, experience story generated during experience activity, they move to convergence space science education room including space laboratory, space workshop, space archives. Based on educational documents of NASA and Aerospace Research Institute , space crew study space science education including gravity flow observation, making the universe gloves, drawing solar system, the existence conditions of extraterrestrial life, extraterrestrial life in my imagination, lunar exploration through discussion, making, experiment to cultivate more detailed understanding, interest, imagination for space science.": 2,
    "Fractal has a shape of which part resembles whole(self-similarity), it has characteristics which this process is repeated endlessly(cyclic).": 2,
    "How the inner structure of the earth formulated By analyzing the speed distribution of the earthquake wave, it is found that the interior of the earth consists of may layers having different physical and chemical properties. In other words, the interior of the earth can be classified into earth crust, mantle, outer nucleus and inner nucleus, which are described in more detail as follows. 1. The earth crust, which is located at outermost region of the earth, is in the layered structure of light and hard rocks, and divided into continent crust and ocean crust. The continent crust is mainly composed of granite with thickness of about 35km, and the ocean crust is composed of basalt with thickness of about 5km. 2. The mantle is a strata located between the crust and the depth of about 2,900km, which is a solid state material heavier than the crust accounting for 82% of the interior volume of the earth. The boundary between the mantle and the crust is called a ＇Mohorovicic discontinuity＇ in which propagation speed of earthquake waves abruptly increase. 3. The outer nucleus is the boundary of the mantle and the inner nucleus, which is considered to be in liquid state. 4. The inner nucleus is under the outer nucleus and located at the center of the earth, which is considered to be in solid state.": 1,
    "Printing technology enabled broadening and popularize knowledge though mass production of books. It is not obvious when printing first started in Korea, but the first printing is carried out by wood type printing. The excellence of Korean printing technology can be known especially from ＇Mugujeonggwangdaedaranigyeong＇, the first wood type printing in the world, and ＇Palmandaejanggyeong＇ which shows the top level technology of wood type printing.": 1,
    "Einstein proved the particle properties of light with experiment on photoelectric effect in which electrons come out as light was exposed to metal, and awarded the Nobel Prize for that. For phenomena by linearity of light around us, there are the Pinhole camera, shadow, solar eclipse and lunar eclipse. For phenomena by reflection of light, there are left-right reversal of the mirror image, image of an object by a camera, reflector, mountain or building reflected in lake, mirage, screen at movie theater and transmission method of optical fiber. Linearity and reflection phenomenon are all applicable to particle properties and wave nature of light, and as the major principles of particle properties, there are Computon Effect and Photoelectric Effect, and for wave nature, there are Huygens principle and de Broglie wavelength.": 1,
    "Let＇s learn about objects around us that utilizes the wave properties of light. We wear sunglasses in order to block lights when driving a car or riding skies. What＇s the example around us that uses the wave properties of lights Why do 3D movies use the principle of polarization of light Lights from lamps or sunlight uniformly contain transverse waves that vibrate in all direction. The polarization plate, however, has the property that penetrates lights vibrating in specific direction, and so, if you see an object through two polarization plates with perpendicular polarization, you cannot see anything. For viewing 3D movies, you should wear polarization glasses which differs in polarization axes in right and left glasses so that different images can be seen for right and left eyes resulting in the sense of stereoscopic images.": 1,
    "Scholar in the field of chemical engineering, who laid grounds for industrial technology and engineering in Korea Ahn Donghyeok is a representative scientist in chemical engineering in Korea, who had leaded the role in establishing the foundations of industrial technology. During Japanese colonial period, he produced lots of research results in fats and oils, and industrial water, and after emancipation, tried to reconstruct and develop industrial technology as the president of Central institute of industry. He also contributed to establishment of many organizations of scientists and engineers such as Association of science, Korean chemistry association and Korean association of ceramics industry. In the corresponding exhibit of Science Museum, related articles are displayed including literature for memorizing 80th birthday of ＇Gyesang＇ Ahn Donghyeok and ＇Bojinjae＇ written by Ahn Donghyeok himself.": 1,
    "Shinjong＇ of Great King Seongdeok, the sound of heaven Shinjong of Great King Seongdeok is a very large bell which was made in Shillar era, with height 3.75m, diameter of the mouth 2.27m, width of 11-25cm and weight of about 18.9 ton, and often called ＇Emile Bell＇ since the sound is similar to the sound of a crying baby. They say a baby was inserted to obtain beautiful sound of the bell, but there is no record of inserting a baby in ＇Samgukyusa＇, a record containing the story of Emile bell. In the corresponding exhibit of Science Museum, visitors can see the phenomena of resonance and beating of the Shinjong through the movie of bell hitting simulator, and learn about the scientific principle lying under the manufacturing of the Shinjong of Great King Seongdeok.": 1
